---
title: Local prompt-library foundation
date: '2026-06-17'
tags:
  - added
summary: The source-run prompt library brought a SvelteKit web UI, Bun API, SQLite store, and early CLI together.
---

This source milestone joined the local SvelteKit library, Bun API, SQLite store,
and CLI. The current app can create and edit prompts, organize them with tags,
groups and favorites, search prompt fields by substring, and copy a saved body.
The local CLI can add, list, search, and print a body by ID.

The old paired stills showed an empty library screen, not a verified populated
prompt workflow. Their visible “ready to deploy” line also implied an install
path that is not implemented. They are withdrawn while real matched light/dark
captures, narrated films, annotations, captions, and posters are produced.
AI-tool installation, semantic search, prompt revisions, and cross-device sync
remain future work. The current API has no account authentication; use a trusted
local environment and review its network exposure before storing sensitive
prompts.
